// datum_units_plane_bare.ri — CLI eval fixture: a BARE plane offset is rejected.
//
// units-length ε (task 5746, R11). `plane_xy(0.0)` passes a dimensionless
// `Real` where a LENGTH is required, so `make_plane` returns `Value::Undef` and
// the post-Undef `geometry_diagnose` hook must emit on stderr:
//   error: plane_xy: offset argument expects Length, got Real; pass a
//   dimensioned length such as `5mm`
// `reify eval` exits NONZERO — the diagnostic is a Severity::Error (C1(iv)),
// which the CLI's pure Severity::Error fold turns into a failing exit code. A
// `Value::Undef` on its own exits 0 (measured: before the classifier arm landed
// this fixture printed `DatumUnitsPlaneBare.p = undef` and exited 0), so the
// Error is the whole user-observable signal.
//
// Zero is deliberately the offset here: it is the one bare magnitude that is
// dimensionally harmless in VALUE (D1), which is exactly why it slipped past the
// pre-doctrine constructor — and it is still a units error, because the
// resulting origin would be a dimensionless Point no LENGTH consumer can use.
//
// Lives in tests/fixtures/ (NOT examples/) since it intentionally fails.
//
// Declares its module explicitly: without it, `reify eval` also emits
// W_MODULE_DECL_MISSING ("expected `module datum_units_plane_bare`"), which
// would re-supply an anchor substring for free and weaken the assertion in
// cli_eval_datum_units.rs.

module datum_units_plane_bare

structure def DatumUnitsPlaneBare {
    let p = plane_xy(0.0)
}
